Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-17-2001||01:10 PM||||Rodney Dickman is the forum  resident expert on Meras.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> im sure hell post here soon. I have a replica myself, Rodney says most kits of 308/328 were pulled off the Mera. There werent very many made. They were custom built by Creative Concepts in Michigan on new cars pulled off the assembly lines and converted then sold thru Pontiac Dealerships.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||XDrewX||08-17-2001||08:20 PM||||ttt<BR>i am also interested||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-18-2001||12:35 AM||||Rodney.......where r u? a few more notes. I think there were only about 275 made from 86-early 88. It was only a body change, drive train, chassis, interior were all left completely stock. think sticker price was around $30,000. After the conversions, they sent all the original body panels back to the assembly line to get put on another new Fiero. The same company that makes real Ferrari wheels specially cast replica ones for Pontiac, and Ferrari threatened to cut them off for it. Then they went after Pontiac in general then to the kit manufacturers.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
